<body>
    <h1>Rectangle Detection</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <h1 id=3D"RectangleDetection-1.IntroductiontoRectangleDetection"><s=
trong>1. Introduction to</strong> Rectangle Detection</h1>
<p>Rectangle detection in images is one of the pillars of computer vision, =
allowing software to interpret and process visual information more efficien=
tly. Among these shapes, rectangles stand out due to their presence in vari=
ous real-world scenarios, such as documents, device screens, and barcodes.<=
/p>
<p>By using the functions provided by the Vision Framework, it=E2=80=99s po=
ssible to detect rectangles in images or videos in a simplified way, and th=
en use their coordinates and dimensions in different kinds of applications.=
</p>
<h3 id=3D"RectangleDetection-PracticalApplications"><strong>Practical Appli=
cations</strong></h3>
<p>Rectangle detection is widely used across various fields of technology, =
including:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Scanning Documents</strong>: Scanner apps use this technology to=
 find the edges of documents and improve the cropping and alignment.</p></l=
i>
<li>
<p><strong>Augmented Reality (AR)</strong>: AR systems detect rectangles to=
 recognize flat surfaces, making it easier to project virtual objects into =
the real world.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Reading Plates and Labels</strong>: Many industrial automation a=
nd logistics solutions use rectangle recognition to identify things like ve=
hicle license plates or product labels.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Medical Image Processing</strong>: Some medical tools use it to =
highlight areas of interest in imaging exams, helping out with diagnosis.</=
p></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"RectangleDetection-What=E2=80=99sVNDetectRectanglesRequest?">What=
=E2=80=99s <code>VNDetectRectanglesRequest</code><strong>?</strong></h3>
<p>Basically, <code>VNDetectRectanglesRequest</code> is a <code>Vision Fram=
ework</code>class that allows the detection of rectangular areas in images,=
 like credit cards, business cards, documents, or signs. It's very useful i=
n document scanning and augmented reality apps.</p>
<p>The class offers configurable properties, such as:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><code>maximumObservations</code>: sets the max number of rectangles it s=
hould try to find</p></li>
<li>
<p><code>minimumConfidence</code>: the lowest confidence level it=E2=80=99l=
l accept for a detection</p></li>
</ul>
<p>By adjusting these parameters, you can optimize detection accuracy and p=
erformance according to the specific needs of your application.</p>
<h3 id=3D"RectangleDetection-What=E2=80=99sVNRectangleObservation?"><strong=
>What=E2=80=99s </strong><code>VNRectangleObservation</code><strong>?</stro=
ng></h3>
<p>When you run a rectangle detection using <code>VNDetectRectanglesRequest=
</code>, the result is a <code>VNRectangleObservation</code> object. This c=
lass represents a rectangle found in an image, providing the normalized coo=
rdinates of its four corners. These coordinates can then be converted to pi=
xel values, enabling precise localization and manipulation of the area of i=
nterest.</p>
<h3 id=3D"RectangleDetection-HowWillWeUseIt?">How Will We Use It?</h3>
<p>Together with functions from AppKit and Foundation, we=E2=80=99ll develo=
p an application that detects documents in an image and identifies the docu=
ment=E2=80=99s edges.</p>
<p>Check out this flow to see how our app will be structured:</p><span clas=
s=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper confluence-embed=
ded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image image-center" alt=
=3D"Untitled - Frame 1 (2).jpg" width=3D"468" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"9383f=
3b052cb0e790343fe70fed111601a25124650609c4fb16c1f48fd5b334d" data-image-src=
=3D"https://developeracademy.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/120887=
7085/Untitled%20-%20Frame%201%20(2).jpg?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D=
1750692274588&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"1045" data-=
width=3D"3824" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=
=3D"1208877097" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-typ=
e=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"Untitled - Frame 1 (=
2).jpg" data-base-url=3D"https://developeracademy.atlassian.net/wiki" data-=
linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/jpeg" data-linked-resource-container-=
id=3D"1208877085" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"1" data-media-i=
d=3D"58830d70-7621-4632-a3b7-594713f4433e" data-media-type=3D"file" height=
=3D"127"></span>
<div class=3D"panel" style=3D"background-color: #E6FCFF;border-width: 1px;"=
>
<div class=3D"panelContent" style=3D"background-color: #E6FCFF;">
<p>Notice that, as mentioned in the Vision Framework intro, we have a base =
structure for using this framework.</p>
</div>
</div>
<h1 id=3D"RectangleDetection-Development">Development</h1>
<p>We=E2=80=99ll build a command-line tool on macOS that follows these step=
s:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Loading the image</strong>: Reads an image from a file.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Processing the image</strong>: Detects rectangles (document edge=
s) using the Vision Framework.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Drawing and exporting</strong>: Draws the detected rectangle on =
the image and saves the result to a new file.</p></li>
</ol>
<p>Let=E2=80=99s break down each step in the code.</p>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"RectangleDetection-Firststep:Loadingtheimage">First step: Loading=
 the image</h3>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: php; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">func loa=
dImage(at path: String) -&gt; NSImage? {
    let fileURL =3D URL(fileURLWithPath: path)
    guard let image =3D NSImage(contentsOf: fileURL) else {
        print("Error: Could not load image.")
        return nil
    }
    return image
}</pre>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"panel" style=3D"background-color: #E6FCFF;border-width: 1px;"=
>
<div class=3D"panelContent" style=3D"background-color: #E6FCFF;">
<p>We convert the <code>NSImage</code> to <code>CGImage</code> so that we c=
an use the <code>VNImageRequestHandler</code>, which requires this format.<=
/p>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: php; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">func nsI=
mageToCGImage(_ image: NSImage) -&gt; CGImage? {
    guard let imageData =3D image.tiffRepresentation,
          let bitmap =3D NSBitmapImageRep(data: imageData) else { return ni=
l }
    return bitmap.cgImage
}</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"RectangleDetection-DetectingRectangles">Detecting Rectangles</h3>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: php; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">func det=
ectDocumentEdges(in image: CGImage, completion: @escaping ([VNRectangleObse=
rvation]?) -&gt; Void) {
    let request =3D VNDetectRectanglesRequest { request, error in
        if let error =3D error {
            print("Error detecting rectangles: \\(error.localizedDescriptio=
n)")
            completion(nil)
            return
        }
        let results =3D request.results as? [VNRectangleObservation]
        completion(results)
    }

    // Parameter tuning for better document detection
    request.minimumAspectRatio =3D 0.5
    request.maximumAspectRatio =3D 1.5
    request.minimumSize =3D 0.2
    request.maximumObservations =3D 1
    request.quadratureTolerance =3D 20.0

    let handler =3D VNImageRequestHandler(cgImage: image, options: [:])
    try? handler.perform([request])
}</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>In this component, we=E2=80=99re integrating <code>VNDetectRectanglesReq=
uest</code> with our handler <code>VNImageRequestHandler</code>. In doing s=
o, we set parameters, such as:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><code>minimumAspectRatio</code> and <code>maximumAspectRatio</code>: Fil=
ters to catch paper-like shapes.</p></li>
<li>
<p><code>minimumSize</code>: Ignores very small detections.</p></li>
<li>
<p><code>maximumObservations</code>: Captures only one document at a time.<=
/p></li>
<li>
<p><code>quadratureTolerance</code>: Allows slight perspective variations.<=
/p></li>
</ul>
<p>Note that the result of our request is a <code>VNRectangleObservation</c=
ode>, a class representing a detected rectangle in an image. Each instance =
of this class provides the coordinates of the rectangle=E2=80=99s four vert=
ices, allowing precise localization of the detected area.</p>
<p>We finish the example with code to draw the detected rectangle on the im=
age:</p>
<h3 id=3D"RectangleDetection-DrawingtheRectangle">Drawing the Rectangle</h3=
>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: php; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">func dra=
wBoundingBox(on image: CGImage, observations: [VNRectangleObservation], out=
putPath: String) {
    let size =3D CGSize(width: image.width, height: image.height)

    guard let colorSpace =3D image.colorSpace else {
        print("Error: No color space found.")
        return
    }

    let context =3D CGContext(
        data: nil,
        width: image.width,
        height: image.height,
        bitsPerComponent: image.bitsPerComponent,
        bytesPerRow: image.bytesPerRow,
        space: colorSpace,
        bitmapInfo: image.bitmapInfo.rawValue
    )

    context?.draw(image, in: CGRect(origin: .zero, size: size))
    context?.setStrokeColor(NSColor.red.cgColor)
    context?.setLineWidth(5)

    for observation in observations {
        let convertedRect =3D VNImageRectForNormalizedRect(observation.boun=
dingBox, image.width, image.height)
        context?.stroke(convertedRect)
    }

    if let newImage =3D context?.makeImage() {
        let outputNSImage =3D NSImage(cgImage: newImage, size: size)
        if let data =3D outputNSImage.tiffRepresentation,
           let bitmap =3D NSBitmapImageRep(data: data),
           let pngData =3D bitmap.representation(using: .png, properties: [=
:]) {
            try? pngData.write(to: URL(fileURLWithPath: outputPath))
            print("Image saved successfully to \\(outputPath)")
        }
    } else {
        print("Error creating image with markings.")
    }
}</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>This utility function is basically a way to give meaning to the result o=
btained from the points of the rectangle formed by the document. We use the=
 following components:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><code>CGContext</code>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>It=E2=80=99s the graphics context where all drawing operations happen. W=
e can think of it as a "screen" or "canvas" where it=E2=80=99s possible to =
draw shapes, images, and text.</p></li>
<li>
<p>In the function, the <code>CGContext</code> is created to have the same =
properties as the original image (width, height, color space, etc.). If the=
 creation fails, the function returns an error.</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><code>VNImageRectForNormalizedRect</code>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>This function converts a normalized rectangle (with values between 0 and=
 1) into actual pixel coordinates of the image.</p></li>
<li>
<p>In the context of the Vision Framework, detections return normalized coo=
rdinates. To draw on the image, it=E2=80=99s necessary to convert them to t=
he image=E2=80=99s coordinate system using this function.</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<div class=3D"panel" style=3D"background-color: #E6FCFF;border-width: 1px;"=
>
<div class=3D"panelContent" style=3D"background-color: #E6FCFF;">
<p>By lowering <code>minimumAspectRatio</code> and <code>minimumSize</code>=
, the detector can identify rectangles that have smaller or more irregular =
dimensions, but still represent meaningful document areas.</p>
<p>Increasing <code>maximumObservations</code> allows for multiple rectangl=
es to be considered, enabling selection of the most appropriate one.</p>
</div>
</div>
<p>And to use the components we created, we have:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: php; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">// Main =
flow: Load image, detect landmarks and draw points
if let nsImage =3D loadImage(at: inputImagePath), let cgImage =3D nsImageTo=
CGImage(nsImage) {
    detectFaceLandmarks(in: cgImage) { faceObservations in
        guard let faceObservations =3D faceObservations, !faceObservations.=
isEmpty else {
            print("No face detected.")
            return
        }
        drawFaceLandmarks(on: cgImage, faceObservations: faceObservations, =
outputPath: outputImagePath)
    }
} else {
    print("Error loading the image.")
}</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>And in this way, we generate a new image from the updated context, conve=
rting this image into the <code>NSImage</code> format and then into PNG dat=
a.</p>
<h3 id=3D"RectangleDetection-Results">Results</h3>
<p>Here=E2=80=99s what we got as a result:</p><span class=3D"confluence-emb=
edded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper confluence-embedded-manual-size"><i=
mg class=3D"confluence-embedded-image image-center" alt=3D"Untitled - Frame=
 2.jpg" width=3D"468" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"8a8f770b491c781f7217de592ed33=
e4ce3d704e9b52c5215d7a07a630fce6984" data-image-src=3D"https://developeraca=
demy.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/1208877085/Untitled%20-%20Fram=
e%202.jpg?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1750692274588&amp;cacheVersion=
=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"1292" data-width=3D"3095" data-unresolved=
-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"1208877100" data-linked-res=
ource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-re=
source-default-alias=3D"Untitled - Frame 2.jpg" data-base-url=3D"https://de=
veloperacademy.atlassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"ima=
ge/jpeg" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"1208877085" data-linked-resou=
rce-container-version=3D"1" data-media-id=3D"6da4a314-9e5e-4ba0-9fa6-803482=
ab855c" data-media-type=3D"file" height=3D"195"></span>
<p>In another example, we have:</p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-=
wrapper image-center-wrapper confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D=
"confluence-embedded-image image-center" alt=3D"Untitled - Frame 3.jpg" wid=
th=3D"468" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"700cc0305aae32d74fcca947fac3c1b6be3641d8=
9bb8518a0c12934945137c94" data-image-src=3D"https://developeracademy.atlass=
ian.net/wiki/download/attachments/1208877085/Untitled%20-%20Frame%203.jpg?v=
ersion=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1750692274588&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;ap=
i=3Dv2" data-height=3D"1292" data-width=3D"3095" data-unresolved-comment-co=
unt=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"1208877103" data-linked-resource-versi=
on=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-defa=
ult-alias=3D"Untitled - Frame 3.jpg" data-base-url=3D"https://developeracad=
emy.atlassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/jpeg" da=
ta-linked-resource-container-id=3D"1208877085" data-linked-resource-contain=
er-version=3D"1" data-media-id=3D"ce52e01b-6ff8-4ef2-a298-65a535a301ec" dat=
a-media-type=3D"file" height=3D"195"></span>
<p><strong>Improving:</strong></p>
<p>Note that in this last example, only part of a document was detected. To=
 achieve better results in such cases, it's important to adjust some proper=
ties.</p>
<p>We tweaked the parameters:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: php; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">    requ=
est.minimumAspectRatio =3D 0.2
    request.minimumSize =3D 0.1
    request.maximumObservations =3D 3 </pre>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"panel" style=3D"background-color: #E6FCFF;border-width: 1px;"=
>
<div class=3D"panelContent" style=3D"background-color: #E6FCFF;">
<p>We improved some detection details, allowing it to find more documents a=
nd detect a larger one.</p>
</div>
</div>
<p>Resulting in:</p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-c=
enter-wrapper confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-emb=
edded-image image-center" alt=3D"Untitled - Frame 3 (1).jpg" width=3D"468" =
loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"e268153926e4490d0ee7e3dc663a6bd69314fe02e36c20dbf0b=
