<h1 id=3D"RectangleDetection-Conclusion">Conclusion</h1>
<p>In this article, we explored how to use the Vision Framework to detect r=
ectangles in images. We covered:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>How to configure and run </strong><code>VNDetectRectanglesReques=
t</code>, understanding its parameters.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>How to draw the detected rectangles</strong> on the image using =
<code>CGContext</code> and convert coordinates with <code>VNImageRectForNor=
malizedRect</code>.</p></li>
</ul>
<p>This Request =E2=86=92 Handler =E2=86=92 Response flow demonstrates the =
modularity of the Vision Framework and its integration with AppKit APIs. Yo=
u can fine-tune the parameters to better fit different detection scenarios,=
 ensuring that your application meets the specific requirements of each pro=
ject.</p>
<p>You can download and test this code from our repository. Try it out in d=
ifferent scenarios and adapt the code according to the results you get.</p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
